      "math_academy_id": "e-3244",
      "problem": "Find the sine of $\\angle Y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224552/assets/e0fb47c85d56c314389a0a334029b3b769f13ddcca6ab15a9021cf6361e4b1ce.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Recall the definition of sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin Y = \\dfrac {\\textrm{opposite}}{\\textrm{hypotenuse}} = \\dfrac {XZ}{YZ} = \\dfrac{XZ}{61}\n$$\n\nHere, we need to determine the missing side $XZ.$ The trick is to use the Pythagorean Theorem:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\nXZ &= \\sqrt{ YZ^2 - XY^2 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{ 61^2 - 60^2 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{ 3721- 3600 } \\\n&= \\sqrt{121 }\\\n&= 11\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\sin Y&= \\dfrac{XZ}{61} = \\dfrac{11}{61}.\n\t}\n$$",
